ves the bottom of node 1, runs down to y ≈ 0.8 cm, runs right to x = 14.2, and rises into the bottom of node 6. Centered label on the horizontal segment, in italics: \"same five observations reused for correction and evaluation\".\n\n**Semantic requirements to preserve**\n- Observed targets and baseline predictions visibly determine the residuals. The residual node is the only point where $y$ and $2x$ meet.\n- The residuals visibly determine the single scalar $b$. The mean node has exactly one incoming arrow from the residual node and produces one scalar output.\n- The scalar $b$ visibly feeds only the corrected prediction, not the baseline and not the targets.\n- The reuse route makes clear that the same five observations are used in both the correction step and the evaluation step.\n- Do not add error bars, confidence intervals, timing values, train/test splits, optimizers, architectures, or external datasets. Do not state or imply generalization or novelty."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3009,"cache_read_input_tokens":2163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3009},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9119bce-a75e-4e67-abe0-e1e86a2841e0","uuid":"34a4d94b-e9f9-4e92-88ac-6e6d827b1c5f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T10:24:50.884Z","request_id":"req_011Ch6Shc1HFnKmFPrXpHtFc"}
